TOTK: last frame's position (patch 0015) for NVN2 (Ampere) vertex shaders. Program.cs turned it off for every Ampere
job because a bank's last-frame slot, bank + 15, can be a slot the shader reads itself: NVN2 shaders read their push
constants as c[24], which is c9's last-frame slot. Without the variant no skinned draw of OoT got its own motion
vectors (the runtime's "position reads other blocks" for all of them). MotionPrevious now looks at the slots the whole
shader reads and declines only a position whose banks need one of them, reporting the banks with location -1 so the
shader's .res.json shows why; every other position gets its copy as on Maxwell. Its bindings are allocated after that
check, in the same order as before, so Maxwell translations stay byte for byte the same.

